<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - Danish Wise Men see fewer jobless in 1997.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Danish Wise Men see fewer jobless in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The independent Danish Economic Council said in its biannual report on Wednesday that it expected a 1997 jobless total of 219,000, 216,000 in 1998 and 209,000 in 1999.</p>
<p>In its previous report last November, the council, known as the Wise Men, forecast 236,000 unemployed in 1997 and 245,000 in 1998.</p>
<p>In 1996, Denmark had an average 8.8 percent unemployment rate, corresponding to 245,600 jobless.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
